%I A401172 #55 Nov 27 2026 22:27:47
%S A401172 2,7,12,17,22,27,32,37,42,48,53,58,63,69,74,79,85,90
%N A401172 a(n) = floor(-log_10(kappa(n))), where kappa(n) is the infimum of Q(f)/||f||^2 over nonzero smooth f(u) supported in (-log(n)/2, log(n)/2), Q being the Weil quadratic form of the Riemann zeta function; a(n) = 0 if kappa(n) <= 0.
%C A401172 Q(f) = 2*Re(F(i/2)*conj(F(-i/2))) + (1/(2*Pi))*Integral_{-oo..oo} (Re(psi(1/4 + i*t/2)) - log(Pi))*|F(t)|^2 dt - Sum_{p^k} 2*log(p)*p^(-k/2)*Re(Integral f(u + k*log(p))*conj(f(u)) du), with F(t) = Integral f(u)*exp(i*t*u) du, ||f||^2 = Integral |f(u)|^2 du, psi = digamma.
%C A401172 Terms for 3 <= n <= 19 are proved by computer-assisted interval bounds (lower bounds: Chekmachev; upper bounds: Wiktorowicz link).
%D A401172 André Weil, Sur les "formules explicites" de la théorie des nombres premiers, Meddel. Lunds Univ. Mat. Sem., Suppl.-band M. Riesz (1952), 252-265.
%H A401172 Vadim Chekmachev, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23848597">Rigorous lower bounds for the truncated Weil form up to support length ln 71 via a lattice minorant</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401172 Rafał Wiktorowicz, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23447302">An Unconditional Exponential Upper Bound for the Windowed Weil Quadratic Form, and Later Versions</a>, Zenodo, 2026 (all versions; Version 9 contains the liminf bound).
%F A401172 If kappa(n) > 0, then a(n) >= floor(4*Pi*n/log(10) - (29/2)*log_10(n) - log_10(3.03*10^6*(1 + 6.4*10^(-11)*sqrt(n)))) for n >= 3.
%Y A401172 Cf. A016873.
%K A401172 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A401172 2,1
%A A401172 _Rafał Wiktorowicz_, Oct 16 2026
